Notifications: NSUserNotificationCenter instead of Growl.

Growl is not bundled: it is defunct, and the source and license of the prebuilt
framework are unidentified (maintainer decision 2026-11-07). iTermGrowlDelegate keeps
its class and selector names, so every caller, the "BM Growl" profile key and saved
Growl triggers are unchanged. It now delivers NSUserNotifications (10.8+) carrying the
same window/tab/view context; a clicked notification is removed from Notification
Center and reveals that session, as before. iTermController creates the delegate at
launch, so clicks on earlier notifications are handled. sticky was Growl-only and is
ignored.

